-- title:
--   n-torsion quotient of a norm-one torus Hopf algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field of characteristic zero, let $c \in K$ be non-zero and not a square in $K$, let $n$ be a prime, and let $\delta$ be an element of the algebraic closure $\overline{K}$ with $\delta^2 = c$ (more precisely, $\delta\cdot\delta$ equals the image of $c$ under the structure map $K \to \overline{K}$). Let $B_0$ be a commutative ring carrying a $K$-Hopf algebra structure whose comultiplication is cocommutative, and let $u_0, v_0 \in B_0$ be such that the $K$-subalgebra generated by $\{u_0,v_0\}$ is all of $B_0$, that $u_0^2 - c\,v_0^2 = 1$, that $\Delta(u_0) = u_0 \otimes u_0 + c\,(v_0 \otimes v_0)$ and $\Delta(v_0) = u_0 \otimes v_0 + v_0 \otimes u_0$, and that for every pair $(w,z) \in \overline{K}^2$ with $w^2 - c z^2 = 1$ there is exactly one $K$-algebra homomorphism $g : B_0 \to \overline{K}$ with $g(u_0) = w$ and $g(v_0) = z$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a type $A$ with a commutative ring structure and a $K$-Hopf algebra structure, cocommutative, together with elements $u', v' \in A$ such that: $\{u',v'\}$ generates $A$ as a $K$-algebra; $u'^2 - c\,v'^2 = 1$; $\Delta(u') = u' \otimes u' + c\,(v' \otimes v')$ and $\Delta(v') = u' \otimes v' + v' \otimes u'$; every $K$-algebra homomorphism $f : A \to \overline{K}$ satisfies $(f(u') + f(v')\delta)^n = 1$; and for every $(w,z) \in \overline{K}^2$ with $w^2 - c z^2 = 1$ and $(w + z\delta)^n = 1$ there is exactly one $K$-algebra homomorphism $f : A \to \overline{K}$ with $f(u') = w$ and $f(v') = z$.
--
--   In geometric terms, $\operatorname{Spec} B_0$ is the norm-one torus of $K(\sqrt{c})/K$ presented by the generators $u_0, v_0$, and $A$ is the coordinate ring of its $n$-torsion subgroup scheme: the statement produces $A$ as a cocommutative Hopf algebra with the same presentation data whose $\overline{K}$-points are exactly the norm-one pairs $(w,z)$ with $(w+z\delta)^n = 1$. It feeds the construction of the finite flat group scheme used on the Galois-representation side of the argument, being cited by [`HopfAlgebra.exists_cocomm_adjoin_nTorsion_quotient_of_normOneTorus_generators`](thm.html#HopfAlgebra.exists_cocomm_adjoin_nTorsion_quotient_of_normOneTorus_generators).
